{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.exists_lawful_Z_with_total_mass_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.exists_lawful_Z_with_total_mass_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L287-L294","doc":"Corollary in the form the gap is usually stated: total mass is **not** `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_total_mass_ne_one_of_badPartitionFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_total_mass_ne_one_of_badPartitionFunction","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L269-L285","doc":"**`Z_pos` alone does not deliver total mass one — witnessed on `measure`\nitself.** `badPartitionFunction` is a lawful `HasPartitionFunction`\ninstance, yet §1's `measure` sums to `1/2` over the whole (one-block)\nindex set.\n\nSo §1's framework, taken alone, cannot call `measure` a probability\nmeasure: the missing content is a value constraint, not a sign constraint.\nThis is exactly why `sum_measure_eq_one_of_Z_eq_sum` must take `hZ` as a\nhypothesis instead of deriving it from `Z_pos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.badPartitionFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.badPartitionFunction","kind":"def","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L263-L267","doc":"A partition function that is **positive but wrong**: it returns `2` where\nthe sum of squares is `1`. It satisfies every constraint\n`HasPartitionFunction` imposes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.unitQDimension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.unitQDimension","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L260-L261","doc":"A one-block q-dimension: the single partition has `d_q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.sum_measure_eq_one_of_Z_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.sum_measure_eq_one_of_Z_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L240-L258","doc":"**The exact axiom `HasPartitionFunction` is missing.** If the opaque `Z k`\nhappens to agree with the constructed sum over `s`, then §1's `measure` does\nhave total mass one. So the gap is precisely this hypothesis: `Z_pos` pins\nthe sign, `hZ` pins the value, and only the latter yields a probability\nmeasure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measureOn_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measureOn_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L227-L232","doc":"Each constructed weight is nonnegative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.qPartitionFunctionOn_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.qPartitionFunctionOn_pos","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L217-L225","doc":"The constructed partition function is positive as soon as one block in `s`\nhas nonvanishing q-dimension — i.e. `Z_pos` is *derivable* here rather than\nassumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.sum_measureOn_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.sum_measureOn_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L203-L215","doc":"**Total mass one** — the statement §1 could not make.\n\nNeeds no ordering on `R'`, only a field and a nonvanishing normaliser. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measureOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measureOn","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L198-L201","doc":"**Constructed q-Plancherel measure**: `d_q(λ)²` normalised by the\nconstructed partition function of `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.qPartitionFunctionOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.qPartitionFunctionOn","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L187-L196","doc":"**Constructed q-Plancherel partition function** over an explicit finite set\nof Wedderburn blocks: `Z_q(s) = Σ_{λ ∈ s} d_q(λ)²`.\n\nUnlike `HasPartitionFunction.Z` this is a *definition*, not an axiom: the\nsummation the class docstring describes is carried out. The `Finset` is\nsupplied by the caller because the universe of partitions of a given size\nis finite but not canonically presented here (the same reason §1 gave for\nleaving `Z` opaque). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.bound","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L151-L151","doc":"The Féray–Méliot `O(1/√k)` bound, for **this** sequence and **its**\nlimit.\n\n`f` and `f_inf` are class *data*, not universally quantified.  They\nwere `∀`-bound until 2026-08-29, which made the class\n**uninhabitable**: `Cq` is fixed by the instance while `f_inf`\nranged over all of `ℝ`, so `f := 0`, `f_inf := Cq + 1`, `k := 4`\n(where `√(4-3) = 1`) gave `Cq + 1 ≤ Cq`, and `False` followed —\nmachine-checked, `#print axioms` clean, in\n`docs/audits/2026-08-29-qplancherel-clt-uninhabitable-probe.lean`.\n\nThe defect was the general shape a sibling branch named on\nPR #6041: *an external theorem asserted for every inhabitant of a\nstructure that does not carry the theorem's hypotheses.*\n[feray2010] Theorem 1.1 is a statement about the q-Plancherel\nbranching fractions, not about arbitrary real sequences, and the\ntype must say so. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.f_inf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.f_inf","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L133-L133","doc":"Its limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.f","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L131-L131","doc":"The branching-fraction sequence the CLT is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.Cq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.Cq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L129-L129","doc":"The constant is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.Cq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.Cq","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The Féray-Méliot constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasQPlancherelCLT","kind":"class","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L120-L151","doc":"**q-Plancherel CLT typeclass**: witnesses the Féray-Méliot\nO(1/√k) bound for q-Plancherel branching fractions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_mul_partitionFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_mul_partitionFunction","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**Measure scales as `d_q²`**: the q-Plancherel measure is\n`d_q(lam)²` divided by the partition function. Specifically,\n`Z_q(k) · measure lam k = d_q(lam)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_eq_zero_of_dq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_eq_zero_of_dq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L90-L97","doc":"**Vanishing on null partitions**: if `d_q(lam) = 0`, then\n`measure lam k = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L83-L88","doc":"**Positivity of the q-Plancherel measure**: every partition has\nnon-negative weight (zero only when `d_q(lam) = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**q-Plancherel measure**: `P_q(lam) = d_q(lam)² / Z_q(|lam|)`.\n\nStated as a function `Λ → ℕ → R` where the second argument is\nthe level `k = |lam|`. The actual constraint that the input\npartition has size `k` is left to the caller. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction.Z_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction.Z_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L70-L70","doc":"`Z(k) > 0` for all `k ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction.Z","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The partition function at level `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.HasPartitionFunction","kind":"class","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L60-L70","doc":"**q-Plancherel partition function** at level `k`:\n`Z_q(k) = Σ_{λ ⊢ k} d_q(λ)²`.\n\nStated as a class field rather than constructed (the\nsummation requires a finite-decidable universe of partitions\nof `k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.QDimension.dq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.QDimension.dq","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The q-dimension of a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.QDimension.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.QDimension.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.QDimension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.QDimension","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QPlancherel.lean#L52-L58","doc":"**q-Dimension typeclass**: a partition type `Λ` carries a\nq-deformed dimension function `d_q : Λ → R`. The classical\ncase `q = 1` recovers the Plancherel dimension `dim λ` (the\nHecke specialisation of the symmetric-group dimension). ","signatureChunk":0}]}